CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* elaborated type in alias template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.  Fixed: the alias template's
type-id is kept unevaluated until instantiation, so tag_t was not declared
and the defaulted template argument `= tag_t' failed ("found no match for
symbol 'box'"); the alias declaration now declares it.
